# Scope-List infi implementation Loop (Long-Running)

**Status**: MANDATORY when the user invokes this workflow

**Orchestration SSOT**: `.cursor/skills/scope-list-implementation-loop/SKILL.md` — multi-scope runs use **scope-orchestrator** agent (sequential or parallel via **scope-worker**).

---

## Non-Negotiable Invariants (HIGHEST PRIORITY)

1. **Do not stop** the outer loop until **every scope** is `DONE` and scope-list items are `[x]`.
2. **Do not skip** a scope because of repeated failures.
3. **Do not ask** for permission to continue between scopes or after failures.
4. **Inner iteration ceiling (3)** exits the tight retry loop only to trigger **RCA + escalation + higher-level re-plan** — then **continue the same scope** until DONE.
5. **Forbidden**: terminal `BLOCKED` that ends the workflow, "workflow finished" with open `[ ]`, or pausing for HITL unless user explicitly aborts.

**Owner checklist** `implementaion_progress_checklist.md` — per `owner-checklist-agent-edits.mdc`: agents may toggle `[x]`, add same-line label, append one-line high-level items; no reorder/delete/subtasks.

---

## Two Loops

- **Inner loop** (per scope): plan → implement → verify → post-impl → governance → review → handoff → assess.
- **Outer loop** (all scopes): next scope only after current scope `DONE`; repeat until no open `[ ]` in scope list file.

When inner `inner_iteration > max_inner_iterations` (default 3): run **Escalation ladder** in the skill (RCA → deep eval → re-plan → reset inner counter → continue). **Never** advance to next scope while current scope incomplete.

---

## Per-Scope Steps

Track `notes/implementations/scope_loop_state.json` and `scope_dag.json` (from `scope_dag.example.json`).

On inner `inner_iteration > max_inner_iterations`: spawn **rca-scope** (E1), then E2–E6 per skill — **never** stop outer loop.

1. PLAN_MODE — plan in `.cursor/plans/` + ADR line when applicable
2. Implement — atomic commits
3. Verify (hard gate) — `build-dev-runner` / `post-implementation-build-dev` (`pnpm build`, `pnpm dev`, dev smoke e2e per `post-implementation-build-dev-verify-loop.mdc`)
4. Post-implementation — `post-implementation-checklist.mdc` and `post-implementation-runner`
5. Governance — `governance-police`
6. Review (hard gate) — `review-scope` / `bugbot`
7. Handoff — `notes/implementations/<plan_base>_brief.txt`
8. Assess — complete → mark scope list `[x]`, next scope; incomplete → inner retry or **escalation** (skill)

---

## Escalation (after 3 inner failures)

Mandatory; does **not** stop outer loop:

1. **RCA** — spawn **rca-scope** (≥3 potential causes; confirmed causes: file proof + confidence > 0.95) → `<scope>_escalation_<N>.txt`
2. **Deep evaluation** — 3-pass scope audit (ADR, rules, boundaries); use `deep-audit-scope-loop` pattern
3. **Higher-level re-plan** — new plan at `escalation_level+1`; split scope if needed; re-read `END-GOAL-PROJECT.md` + relevant ADRs
4. **Structure-reader** if path/SSOT issue
5. **Unblock dependencies** (env, services, submodule) — fix and retry verify
6. Reset `inner_iteration=1`, increment `escalation_level`, continue same scope

At `escalation_level >= 3`: add code-quality review on scope diff; consider ADR update if architecture was wrong.

---

## Stop Condition (only)

- All scopes `DONE` and scope list fully `[x]`, **or**
- User explicitly aborts

Final summary: scopes DONE, escalation count per scope, latest brief, any remaining `last_failure` if user aborted mid-run.

---

## Quick Reference

| Phase | Action |
|-------|--------|
| Inner | Plan → implement → gates → assess |
| Inner retry | Up to 3 same-approach cycles |
| Escalation | RCA → audit → re-plan → reset inner → continue |
| Outer | Next scope only when current DONE |
| Stop | All DONE or user abort only |

